  "interpretation_corrections": [
    "V mean Haversine distance cannot determine T standardized coordinate MSE; first-100-update averaged loss does not establish first-update baseline or continuous departure. No conclusion that position standardized MSE is intrinsically insensitive to meter error is supported.",
    "076B beats 074C pooled position metrics but all 300 scenes and 38 components have worse MAE than its own fixed physical position initial state; retain the preregistered stop condition.",
    "076B speed MAE gain over 074C occurs in only 152/300 scenes; heading MAE gains in 185/300 scenes but 19/38 components. Not uniformly improved all-attribute recovery.",
    "076B vs 072C speed and heading compares learned PTFM outputs with unchanged Mean control attributes, not a Transformer trained for speed or heading.",
    "076A within-target speed dynamics findings belong to 074C weights; cannot inherit them as an actual measured 076B dynamics result.",
    "Scene3035 contributes 103.12 percent of pooled SSE gain versus 074C; excluding it reverses RMSE ordering, with MAE gain retained. This is sensitivity analysis only, not a replacement ranking or justification to discard difficult targets."
  ],
